qembian: TLB work for Symbian on ARMv6 (docs/perf.md "QEMU TLB").

- accel/tcg/cputlb.c: per-ASID TLB contexts. An ASID change parks the current softmmu TLB and
  jump cache (16 slots, LRU) instead of flushing; page invalidations, code-page protection and
  translation cache flushes reach the parked contexts; any other flush drops them.
  SYBORG_ASID_TLB=0: off.
- DACR writes (ARMv6): TLB entries record their short-descriptor domain (ptw.c); only domains
  whose access level falls are dropped (and the jump cache when code ever ran from them), not the
  whole TLB. SYBORG_DACR_TRACK=0: off.
- target/arm/cpu.c: ARMv6 uses 4K target pages like v7 (no tiny pages; XP=1 guests have no 1K
  subpage permissions; ptw.c warns otherwise). SYBORG_V6_1K_PAGES=1: 1K pages.
- TB_JMP_CACHE_BITS 12 -> 14.

